15 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Panel A illustrates a schematic workflow for a clinical study on electrochemotherapy \(ECT\), depicting sample collection from patients at different time points, followed by tissue sectioning and spatial transcriptomics analysis. Panel B displays bar and violin plots quantifying total cells and transcript counts per cell across samples from three patients at multiple time points, both pre- and post-ECT. Panel C presents a stacked bar chart showing the relative proportions of various cell types in each sample, color-coded by cell type. Panel D contains spatial maps illustrating cell type distributions in tissue sections from patients A, B, and C at different time points, highlighting changes following ECT treatment.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a UMAP plot categorizing malignant cell types by color. Panel B displays another UMAP plot coded by cell cycle phase, alongside bargraphs of cell cycle phase proportions across patients and conditions. Panel C containsUMAP density plots comparing embedding at different treatment days. Panel D is a UMAPplot colored by pseudotime progression. Panel E presents a heatmap of gene andpathway scores across cells sorted by pseudotime, indicating changes in expression andcell state. Panel F displays spatial maps of representative tumour tissue regions across different treatment conditions, highlighting malignant cell subpopulations, functional scores, and gene expression patterns. Panel G is a bar chart of log2 fold changes in cell types near malignant cells. Panel H shows spatial maps of malignant-cell-enriched tumour regions, with individual cells colored according to their cell type annotations. Panel I is a dot plot of gene expression in keratinocytes bordering malignant cells at two distance categories.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Panel-based scientific figure illustrating immune cell profiling across patients A, B, and C, featuring stacked area plots, multiple UMAP visualizations, boxplot gene expression summaries, activation and immunosuppressive scores, and scatter plots comparing T cell and myeloid cell subtypes, gene marker expression, and population ratios under different treatment and control conditions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A contains six radar charts, each representing different tissue niches: malignant immune-hot, malignant immune-cold, immune-active, necrotic, healthy epithelium, and stromal, with colored outer rings indicating proportions of various cell types and radar plots showing values for proliferation, immune infiltration, regulation, matrix activity, and angiogenesis. Panel B shows histology or tissue maps for three patients at different time points and treatments, with each niche color-coded as per the legend. Panel C presents a stacked bar chart comparing niche proportions over time and post-treatment for each patient using the same color scheme.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays spatial maps illustrating different tissue niches and inflammatory scores for three patients\220 tumor samples, marked with selected regions of interest. Panel B shows a line graph of standardized inflammatory score versus distance to the immune front, with curves for each patient. Panel C presents kernel density plots of inflammatory score distributions for each patient. Panel D offers zoomed-in images for each region of interest, indicating niche categories, local inflammatory scores, and annotated cell types. Panel E features a bar chart comparing the percentage of T cell-infiltrated malignant immune-hot areas among patients. Panel F displays three sets of spatial maps highlighting single-cell expression of specific marker genes\204GZMB in T cells, CXCL9 in myeloid cells, and POSTN in fibroblasts. Panel G uses a bubble chart to compare expression levels and proportions of cells expressing key genes across cell types and patients.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
